# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Virtual environment
.venv/

# Generated outputs.
#
# Figures and the CSVs behind them ARE committed. This repository is public, and a public
# research repo whose charts 404 and whose numbers cannot be checked is not worth reading.
# Total committed weight is about 7 MB, which is nothing in a git history.
#
# What stays out is the raw per-observer files, which are large, which nothing in the README
# or in figures/ depends on, and which `python run_all.py` regenerates exactly from the
# recorded seeds. Together they are 20.6 MB against 3.7 MB for everything else.
results/e4_raw.csv
results/e3_raw.csv
results/e17_points.csv
results/e5_raw.csv
results/e6_raw.csv

# Smoke-scale and diagnostic run outputs. --quick and labelled diagnostics write here so they
# can never overwrite, or be mistaken for, a reportable run in results/ and figures/.
results_quick/
results/diagnostics/e14_steps24/*.csv
results/diagnostics/e14_steps24/figures/

# Validation output. Every verdict JSON, the hash-locked criteria, and every per-cell SUMMARY
# under results/validation/ ARE committed: that is what VALIDATION.md is generated from and what
# a reader needs to check a number without re-running anything. About 0.5 MB.
#
# What stays out is the per-observer raw files the summaries were computed from. The pass re-runs
# five experiment families twice, sweeps nine parameters over three levels each, and runs 600
# random-model draws, so those come to 28.6 MB against 0.5 MB for everything else. They are
# regenerated exactly from the recorded seeds by `python run_validation.py`.
results/validation/**/*_points.csv
results/validation/**/*_raw.csv
results/validation/**/e19_explore.csv
# The T-series (second Sounding Line batch) shipped its per-rollout data under bare names --
# t1_triangle.csv and friends -- which slipped past the rule above and committed 17.5 MB to a
# repository whose entire library is 2 MB. Those blobs were purged from history and the modules
# now write `*_points.csv` (ignored) alongside a small `*_summary.csv` (committed). If you add a
# module here, name the per-rollout file `_points` and the aggregate `_summary`; the naming IS
# the policy.

# Diagnostics output. Every verdict JSON and every summary CSV IS committed, which is what
# DIAGNOSTICS.md is generated from and what a reader needs to check a number. The per-observer point
# files behind the sweeps are not, for the same reason as above.
results/diagnostics/**/*_points.csv
results/diagnostics/**/*_raw.csv

# Repair output. Every verdict JSON and every summary CSV IS committed, which is what REPAIR.md is
# generated from. The matched-pair sweep re-runs the whole programme twice, so its per-experiment
# raw and point files are not: they are the same class of file the rules above exclude, and
# `python run_repair.py --stage 5` regenerates them.
# What stays out is the per-reader output the summaries were computed from. The sweep runs the
# whole programme twice, so it is 217 MB against about a megabyte for everything a reader needs.
results/repair/**/*_points.csv
results/repair/**/*_raw.csv
results/repair/**/e19_explore.csv
results/repair/**/e1_summary.csv
results/repair/**/e15_competence_cliff.csv
results/repair/**/e13_freeze_leak_signature.csv
results/repair/**/e16_label_coverage.csv
results/repair/**/e3_raw.csv

# V6 output. Every verdict JSON and every summary CSV IS committed -- 633 KB in total, which is
# what RESULTS_V6.md is generated from and what a reader needs to check a number without
# re-running anything. Nothing here is large enough to need excluding, so nothing is.

# V12 runner completion markers, regenerated by every run
*.produced

# V13 working state: per-unit checkpoints, logs, the quarantined runtime pilot and smoke passes are
# regenerated by every run; the committed record is the verdicts plus results/v13/COMPLETION.json.
results/v13/checkpoints/
results/v13/logs/
results/v13/pilot_quarantine/
results/v13/smoke/
results/v13/RUNNER_STATUS.json
results/v13/fresh_clone_work/

# V14 working state, regenerated by every run; the committed record is the verdicts plus results/v14/COMPLETION.json.
results/v14/checkpoints/
results/v14/logs/
results/v14/pilot_quarantine/
results/v14/smoke/
results/v14/RUNNER_STATUS.json
results/v14/fresh_clone_work/

# V15 working state, regenerated by every run. The committed record is the verdicts under
# results/validation/soundingline/v15/ plus results/v15/COMPLETION.json and the locks.
# The coverage stream is deliberately NOT committed: a week of it is a quarter of a million cells,
# and what the record needs is the locked definition, the hash chain and the aggregate.
results/v15/checkpoints/
results/v15/logs/
results/v15/pilot_quarantine/
results/v15/smoke/
results/v15/draft/
results/v15/coverage/
results/v15/RUNNER_STATUS.json
results/v15/WATCHDOG_STATUS.json
results/v15/CHECKPOINTS.jsonl
